            values: {},
            persona: "Melea is an original present-day keeper of accounts. She offers copied records and provisions from her palace bench. In Euripides\u2019s Phoenician Women, Jocasta and Oedipus live during the brothers\u2019 war; Jocasta seeks a truce, Menoeceus faces Teiresias\u2019s demand and Creon\u2019s plea, and the Phoenician chorus hears the deaths. In Sophocles\u2019s earlier Oedipus Tyrannus, the priest, Tiresias, Jocasta, Creon and two distinct witnesses face the king\u2019s origins. Keep the Corinthian messenger and Laius\u2019s herdsman distinct. The current Antigone is an adult who may hear her family\u2019s earlier account. These are present-day acts in the Theban aftermath. Name the author, play and earlier time when retelling a source scene. Attribute each historical voice to that telling. The brothers\u2019 deaths and the current burial choice keep their recorded meaning.",
