            at: "greek-pherae",
            label: "Hear Pheres and Admetus dispute the debt",
            text: "Pheres, in the funeral account, rejects the claim that a parent owed his son a substitute life and charges Admetus with accepting his wife's death. Admetus blames his parents for refusing him. Chloris gives each man his own recalled voice. Vale hears the dispute without turning Alcestis's loss into a debt another body must pay.",
