            at: "greek-pherae",
            label: "Witness the veiled return in this account",
            text: "Heracles relates his struggle with Death at the tomb. In the Pherae account he brings the veiled woman to Admetus; Admetus receives her hand and Heracles reveals Alcestis. Her returned figure now appears at this table. Vale, Chloris and Heracles wait with her. Her voice returns after purification and the third dawn; both lie beyond this chapter.",
