            label: "Hear Pelasgus answer the herald",
            text: "Melia tells Vale the next part of the older account. The Egyptian herald demanded the Danaids and threatened to drag them to the ship. Pelasgus confronted him and upheld the Argive resolve against forced surrender. He then offered public lodgings and rooms of his own, asking the women to choose. Danaus returned with an Argive escort. The play leaves their future open. Melia asks the present hosts to keep their own promise to Nera.",
